---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CategoryStrip from '../components/CategoryStrip.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
import Doc from '../components/Doc.astro';

/**
 * Privacy, written for what the site actually is: static pages with no
 * accounts or forms, with Google Analytics for audience measurement.
 * Keep this page in step with the tracking in the shared Layout.
 */
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy — OSI Affiliate"
  description="How OSI Affiliate uses Google Analytics, what the hosting provider logs, and what happens when you follow a vendor link."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <CategoryStrip />
  <main id="main">
    <PageHead
      title="Privacy"
      lede="This site is a set of static pages with no accounts, comment forms or newsletter. We use Google Analytics to understand visits and how readers use the site. Here is what that involves."
    />

    <Doc>
      <section>
        <h2>What we collect</h2>
        <p>
          We use Google Analytics to measure page views, visits, traffic sources and interactions
          such as scrolling and clicks on links to other sites. Google Analytics uses cookies to
          distinguish browsers and visits, and receives information such as the pages visited,
          referring site, browser and device details. We review reports to improve the site.
        </p>
        <p>
          Our Analytics tag disables Google signals and advertising personalization. We do not
          send names or email addresses to Analytics. The search box works inside your browser;
          its search text is not sent to us by the search feature.
        </p>
        <p>
          See <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>.
          You can block Analytics with browser privacy tools or use{' '}
          <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" rel="noopener">Google's Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What the host logs</h2>
        <p>
          The site is served by Cloudflare, which keeps standard web server logs (the address a
          request came from, the page requested, the time, and the browser's user-agent string) for
          security and to keep the site up. Those logs are Cloudflare's, held under
          <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>,
          and we do not use them to identify visitors.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Vendor links</h2>
        <p>
          When you follow a link to a vendor's site, you leave this one. Some of those links carry
          an affiliate tag, which tells the vendor the visit came from here so that a commission can
          be paid if you sign up; the tag does not identify you to us, and what the vendor collects
          from then on is covered by the vendor's own policy. The
          <a href="/disclosure">affiliate disclosure</a> says which links these are.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Email</h2>
        <p>
          If you email the desk, we keep the message for as long as it is useful for answering it
          and for correcting the page it was about. We do not add you to any list.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          If the site starts collecting anything it does not collect today, this page will say so
          before it happens. Questions go to the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </Doc>
  </main>
</Layout>
